  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/pseudocrenilabrus-philander-dispersus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Reaches 6–8 cm. Easy to keep and breed, a mouthbrooder with splendid coloration.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/pseudocrenilabrus-philander-dispersus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Due to its small size the fish needs no large aquarium. It can be kept very well in planted tanks, as the fish do not harm the plants.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/pseudocrenilabrus-philander-dispersus-2/",
      "html": "<p>One should not underestimate the potential for aggressiveness in this golden flasher. One should never keep delicate or sensitive fish along with them.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/25-perchlike-fishes/pseudocrenilabrus-philander-dispersus-2/",
      "html": "<p>Some years later – 1911 – a similar species was imported. It became somewhat larger (5-6 cm in P. multicolor, 6-8 cm in the new species) and was determined as Pseudocrenilabrus philander dispersus or Brass Mouthbrooder, sometimes also as Southern Mouthbrooder. This species is much nicer in respect of coloration, but as easy to keep and breed as its cousin.</p>"
    }
  ],
